$$Cov = \begin{pmatrix}
Var(x) & Corr(x,y) * Cov(x,y) \\
Corr(x,y) * Cov(x,y) & Var(y)
\end{pmatrix}$$
where $Var(x)$ and $Var(y)$ are the variances of $x$ and $y$, respectively, and $Cov(x,y)$ is the covariance between $x$ and $y$.

Given the variances:
$$Var(x) = (1+4+9+16) / 4 = 30 / 4 = 7.5$$
$$Var(y) = (9+25+9+9) / 4 = 52 / 4 = 13$$

