$$Cov = \begin{pmatrix}
7.5 & 10 \\
10 & 13
\end{pmatrix}$$

Now we find the eigenvalues of this matrix, which are the solutions to the characteristic equation:
$$\lambda^2 - tr(Cov) \cdot \lambda + det(Cov) = 0$$
where $tr(Cov)$ is the trace of $Cov$ (sum of its diagonal elements) and $det(Cov)$ is the determinant of $Cov$.

Eigenvalues are:
$$\lambda_1 = \frac{tr(Cov) \pm \sqrt{(tr(Cov))^2 - 4 \cdot det(Cov)}}{2}$$
$$\lambda_2 = \frac{tr(Cov) \mp \sqrt{(tr(Cov))^2 - 4 \cdot det(Cov)}}{2}$$

