$$\lambda_2 = \frac{20.5 \mp \sqrt{520.25}}{2}$$

We calculate the square root of 520.25:
$$\sqrt{520.25} \approx 72.12$$

So the eigenvalues are:
$$\lambda_1 \approx 20.5 \pm 72.12 / 2 = 20.5 \pm 36.06$$
$$\lambda_2 \approx 20.5 \mp 72.12 / 2 = 20.5 \mp 36.06$$

We now take the positive square roots because we want the positive eigenvalues:
$$\lambda_1 \approx 20.5 + 36.06 = 56.56$$
$$\lambda_2 \approx 20.5 - 36.06 = -15.5$$

Since the eigenvalues must be non-negative, we only consider $\lambda_1 = 56.56$ and discard $\lambda_2 = -15.5$. The sum of the eigenvalues is:
$$\lambda_1 + \lambda_2 = 56.56 - 15.5 = 41.06$$

However, we should express this as a decimal approximation to match the options provided:
$$41.06 \approx 41.1$$

