$D_x = 8 \cdot (32 - 4) - 12 \cdot (8 - 4) + 1 \cdot (4 - 4)$

$D_x = 8 \cdot 28 - 12 \cdot 4 + 1 \cdot 0$

$D_x = 224 - 48$

$D_x = 176$

Now, we replace the second column with the constants to find Dy:

$D_y = 2 \cdot (1 \cdot 8 - 1 \cdot 1) - 3 \cdot (8 \cdot 8 - 4 \cdot 1) + 1 \cdot (4 \cdot 1 - 8 \cdot 1)$

